From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Share a table's spare width between columns in proportion
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The maximise step of grid track sizing gives every track an equal share
of the free space until it reaches its growth limit. Table columns do
not grow that way. css-tables-3 §3.9.4 interpolates between sizing
guesses, which moves every column the same fraction of the way from its
minimum to its maximum width.

With equal shares, narrow columns reach their maximum first and the wide
column gets the rest. On a Wikipedia table beside floated figures, the
date and length columns kept their full widths and the description
column was squeezed to a few words per line.

Add GridContainerStyle::is_table_grid. When it is true, the maximise
step weights each column by the room it has left to grow.
